# v2.7.6: DSV41_GREEDY_NOGATHER=1 (adapter/greedy_nogather.py): every draft and target-verify CUDA graph shape gets a
# second "greedy flavour", replayed on steps whose batch is all greedy. The draft flavour runs the sharded greedy Markov
# step (per-rank (max, argmax), one compact gather) instead of all-gathering the full [bs x 5, V] step logits; the target
# flavour all-gathers one (max, argmax) pair per 4096 vocab columns instead of the [M, V] verify logits and hands the
# argmax ids to the in-graph greedy accept. Sampled steps, logprobs, grammar / penalties and the draft-capture tap keep
# the stock graphs. Emitted tokens are exact (greedy verification accepts the target's argmax). In-boot A/B against
# v2.7.5 (tier-12o window n, official 1017): c16 -2.28 ms/step [-3.85, -0.71], c4 -0.86 ms/step [-1.44, -0.28], qeval
# 75 / 75 inside the T = 0 bracket, draft acceptance bit-identical to both controls. The flavours are one more capture of
# every draft / verify shape (head low-water 5.19 GiB against 5.76 / 5.73 GiB in the release gate). Release gate against
# two v2.7.5 controls: greedy c1 x1.012, c4 x1.018, c8 x1.026, c16 x1.029 of the slower control, c1 step -0.31 ms
# (paired); verdict INVALID through a new host-job rule, reviewed as release-equivalent (see CHANGELOG.md).
# Rollback, config only: unset DSV41_GREEDY_NOGATHER (= the v2.7.5 profile; the image is the same).
# v2.7.7: DSV41_DRAFT_HEAD_FP4=1 (adapter/draft_head_fp8.py, needs DSV41_DRAFT_HEAD_FP8=1): beside the fp8 twin of the
