_TABLE=1 DSV41_PREFILL_MOE_FOLD=1 DSV41_WO_A_CFG_TABLE=1 DSV41_MOE_SCALE_CODES=1 DSV41_MOE_SCALE_CODES_MIN_ROWS=2 DSV41_MOE_EVICT_FIRST=1 DSV41_L2_PREFETCH_SHPF_MB=6 DSV41_L2_PREFETCH_SHPF_EL=0 DSV41_GREEDY_NOGATHER=1 DSV41_DRAFT_HEAD_FP4=1"
# Production settings, together with the line above.
# Measured only on the canary-roce production line (bounded indexer on); do not use 8192 on the other images.
#CHUNKED_PREFILL_SIZE=8192
# THE MEMORY FRACTION (one parameter, both lines equal; it goes with the pool pin below):
#MEM_FRACTION_STATIC=0.85
#HEAD_MEM_FRACTION_STATIC=0.85
#EXTRA_SGLANG_ARGS="--fp8-gemm-backend flashinfer_cutlass --watchdog-timeout 1800 --min-free-slots-delay 1 --enable-deepseek-v4-fp4-indexer --enable-cache-report --sleep-on-idle --swa-prefix-tails 384 --prefill-decode-interval 2"
# v2.6.5: the v41n KV pool pinned at 8,541,952 tokens (8.15 x 1M; 7.26 GiB of KV per rank at 912.25 B per token) at
# fraction 0.85 (at 0.78 v41n's budget is ~6.1-6.2M tokens, so the pin would not bind). Measured on the four Sparks
# (memory ladder 2026-11-06): SAFE with eight 1M-token prompts resident at once, a cold 1M prefill and a long-prompt
# soak, head low-water 5.72 GiB, NVRM 2 (two worker lines in the 8 x 1M cell), speed within 0.6 % of v2.6.4 (8,000,000:
# SAFE, 5.96 GiB; 5,130,752 at 0.78: 8.87-9.32 GiB). The fraction gives the 8192-token prefill chunk less spare memory
# than 0.78 did; the 1M prefills of that run passed at it. Keep the pin a multiple of 256 (the KV page).
# THE POOL PIN (one parameter; it goes with THE MEMORY FRACTION above):
#MAX_TOTAL_TOKENS=8541952

# Optional NCCL per-HCA RoCEv2 GID selection when address lookup has no result.
# Default off preserves the recipe's fallback index 3. An explicit
# NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX always wins; qualify automatic selection on the fleet.
#NCCL_IB_GID_AUTO=1

# Optional persistent, node-local Triton cache in each rank's state volume.
# Default off; to be qualified on the fleet (boot and first-request latency).
#DSV41_TRITON_CACHE=1

# Experimental small-request admission during an in-flight chunked prefill.
# Requires canary images (Dockerfile.canary / Dockerfile.canary-roce);
# the stock-base Dockerfile does not support it.
# Default unset = off. Add DSV41_PREFILL_BYPASS=<max fresh prompt tokens> to
# EXTRA_CONTAINER_ENV identically on every rank, e.g. DSV41_PREFILL_BYPASS=256.
# This is also the total extra fresh-token budget for one chunk pass. The
# deterministic scan is capped at 32 waiting candidates; optionally set
# DSV41_PREFILL_BYPASS_SCAN=<positive count> identically on every rank.
# The engine's token-pool memory check remains mandatory; skipped/oversized
# candidates stay in queue. Ordinary TP only; extra cache/LoRA/preemption modes
# are excluded.
# GPU and TP4 fleet qualification are still pending.
# Solo short pass (needs DSV41_PREFILL_BYPASS; in the production profile since
# v2.6.2): DSV41_PREFILL_BYPASS_SOLO=1 runs one admitted short request in a pass
# of its own instead of beside the chunk; the parked long prompt resumes alone in
# the next pass with the same chunk (its chunks, boundaries and numerics stay
# those of an idle run). Each solo pass and resume logs one DSV41_SOLO_RECEIPT
# line. Set it identically on every rank; unset or 0 is v2.6.1's bypass.
# Optional companion: append --prefill-decode-interval 2 to EXTRA_SGLANG_ARGS.
# Decode gaps can reduce small-chat latency during long prefills, at the cost
# of cold-prefill throughput. No cadence or chunk-size default is changed.
# Decode yield (canary images; off by default): DSV41_DECODE_YIELD=<1..90> in
# EXTRA_CONTAINER_ENV, identically on every rank. After a non-final chunk of a long prompt
# with other streams decoding, prefill waits until the streams have had pct/(100-pct) of
# the chunk's (modelled, integer, no clock) time: 33 = streams at ~1/3 speed instead of
# ~1/14 during a long prefill, that prompt's first token ~1.4x later (50: ~1/2 speed,
# ~1.9x). Only when the next chunk runs changes (chunks and batches are the engine's own).
# Works on top of --prefill-decode-interval (never fewer steps than it). Unset or 0 = off.
# DSV41_DECODE_YIELD_RID_ARMS is a test-only switch. In the production profile since
# v2.6.4 at share 33: two 300K streams beside a cold 500K prefill on 4 Sparks kept 0.393
# of their decode rate (stock 0.080), the 500K prompt's first token x1.47 later.
# Canary images also expose the source-qualified SGLang #44001 gate. For example,
# append --prefill-decode-interval-min-bs 4 so the interval is skipped while the
# live batch has 0-3 requests and applies from four requests onward. Default 0
# preserves the old cadence. This still needs a GB10 multi-user A/B before promotion.
